# GpxCompare trace profile (not shipped): follows a given line through dense via points so its BRouter way tags
# can be read. Every way with a highway tag (and ferries) costs the same, access / oneways / elevation / turns are
# ignored: between two via points ~150 m apart the shortest way is the line itself. Not for real routing.

---context:global
assign validForBikes = true
assign validForFoot = true
assign processUnusedTags = true
assign turnInstructionMode = 0
assign downhillcost = 0
assign uphillcost = 0

---context:way
assign turncost = 0
assign initialcost = 0
assign costfactor = if and highway= not route=ferry then 10000
                    else if highway=proposed|abandoned then 10000
                    else 1

# include smoothness in the way tags (as trekking.brf)
assign dummyUsage = smoothness=

---context:node
assign initialcost = 0
